# Git Hygiene

- Inspect status before broad edits. Preserve unrelated user work.
- Do not reset, checkout, clean, rebase, force-push, or rewrite history unless explicitly requested.
- Keep changes focused; avoid drive-by formatting of unrelated files.
- Review the final diff for unintended files, generated artifacts, debug code, and secrets.
- Commit messages should describe intent and remain consistent with repository conventions.
